{%- comment -%}
  robots.txt

  There was no robots.txt.liquid in this theme at all, which means the store has
  been serving Shopify's default. That default is not hostile — it allows
  crawling and points at the sitemap — but it says nothing explicit about AI
  crawlers, and "not mentioned" is a weaker position than "named and allowed"
  when an operator is deciding whether a site wants to be read.

  Built on top of Shopify's own default rather than replacing it. The
  `robots.default_rules` object emits everything Shopify maintains — the
  /checkout, /cart, /account, /admin and internal-search disallows, plus the
  Sitemap line — so this file adds to that instead of hand-copying a list that
  would go stale the moment Shopify changes it. Replacing it wholesale is the
  usual way people accidentally expose checkout URLs to crawlers.

  The AI groups below are additive and deliberately permissive: NON's case is
  that the catalogue and the pairing logic should be quotable by an answer
  engine. Each is named explicitly because these agents do not reliably inherit
  User-agent: * — several publishers have found the opposite, and a named group
  is unambiguous.

  Reachable at /robots.txt once deployed. Note Shopify serves this from the
  PUBLISHED theme only, so it will not take effect until this theme is live.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- for group in robots.default_groups -%}
  {{- group.user_agent }}
  {%- for rule in group.rules -%}
    {{ rule }}
  {%- endfor -%}
  {%- if group.sitemap != blank -%}
    {{ group.sitemap }}
  {%- endif -%}
{%- endfor -%}

# --- AI answer engines -------------------------------------------------------
# Named explicitly rather than left to inherit User-agent: *. The same
# checkout/account paths Shopify disallows above are repeated here, because a
# named group replaces the wildcard group for that agent rather than adding to
# it — omitting them would hand these crawlers the URLs the default protects.

User-agent: GPTBot
Disallow: /admin
Disallow: /cart
Disallow: /orders
Disallow: /checkouts/
Disallow: /checkout
Disallow: /account
Disallow: /search
Allow: /

